    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7495" root="حذى" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُذَيَّا</span></b>  <i>A gift,</i> or <i>present, for bringing good
news.</i> (K, TA.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِذْيَةٌ</span>. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْذَهُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِيْنَ الحُذَيَّا وَالخُلْسَةِ</span> <i>He took it as something between a gift and a thing carried off by force.</i>
(ISd, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُذْيَا</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ حُذَيَّاكَ</span>: see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِذَآءٌ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حذو</span>.

